Z||000014||BluByYou||07-22-99||10:25 AM||||Jay, I also have an '87 GT.  Mine has the factory wing and is really clean.  I paid $6500 for it 3 yrs ago when it had 27,500 miles, and only one owner.  I think when it comes to these cars it's a subjective issue.  It's like hotrods - they're not worth much to anyone else, but to an enthusiast, well, you've seen what guys are willing to pay.  So the question is .... How quick do you want to get rid of it?  If you can wait, you'll get your $6k, I'm sure.  By the way, WHY ARE you getting rid of it?  In terms of bang-for-the-buck, I think these cars are top notch.  Couldn't touch anything else as fun for the same money.
