Z||000019||batboy||07-25-99||03:32 PM||||If I recall about Fiero recalls (pun intended) there were more than one. The heat shield one is a biggie, but I think some models had a parking brake recall too. I wonder if they were thinking about one recall and not the other or something. Laziness may have something to do with it too. I've had nothing but bad luck when dealing with dealerships (another intentional pun) and now I will go out of my way to avoid them. I know one or two of the forum regulars work at dealerships, so nothing personal...there must be good ones out there. It's just after getting burnt a few times, I'm overly cautious. If I were you, I'd go back and insist that they do the recall, they have to do it by law, regardless of whether they think it's necessary or not. If they give you the run around, give them hell...that usually works for me. The more customers that are around, the louder I get. They usually will do about anything to shut you up at that point. You have to stick up for yourself, because nobody else will, that's for sure.
